; Shared PWeb application-payload include (CAP-6b4 extraction of the
; release triple out of tools/setup/pwebappsetup.issi).
;
; This file authors, ONCE, the only [Files] entries that install the
; application itself - the unchanged CAP-6 release triple:
;
;   releaseapp.exe  the release host (the same source built per mode:
;                   only the fixed profile compiles it with
;                   -dPWEB_FIXED_RUNTIME)
;   app.pwb         the bundle - byte-identical across all profiles
;   webview.dll     the pinned binding - byte-identical across all
;                   profiles
;
; It is a SEPARATE include from the identity one for exactly one
; reason, measured against the pinned ISCC 6.7.3: the position of these
; three entries inside a profile's [Files] order decides what a FAILED
; profile switch leaves behind.
;
;   common payload BEFORE the fixed profile's verdict gate (the
;   pre-CAP-6b4 order): a failed Evergreen -> fixed switch exits
;   nonzero and Inno's rollback removes the runtime tree - but the
;   source install's releaseapp.exe has already been OVERWRITTEN with
;   the fixed-mode binary, leaving a fixed-mode app with no runtime
;   tree and a marker still reading the source profile. A mixed,
;   broken install.
;
;   common payload AFTER the verdict gate (the ratified order): the
;   gate aborts before these entries are ever reached, so the source
;   install's payload, marker and uninstall registration are
;   byte-identical to pre-switch.
;
; Both source profiles are measured, not one: the CAP-6b4 matrix runs
; a failing post-install gate over an OFFLINE install (row F3) and over
; a NORMAL install (row F3b), and asserts byte-identity of the source
; triple in each.
;
; So each profile #includes this file at the position ITS order needs -
; the Evergreen profiles right after their own dontcopy payload, the
; fixed profile after its verdict entry - while the entries themselves
; can never fork between profiles. The fixed profile's gate is not
; weakened by this: it still runs after the entire runtime tree has
; landed, which is the only thing it verifies.
;
; Consumed define (validated by pwebappsetup.issi, which every profile
; includes before this one):
;   PWEB_PAYLOAD_DIR  staged payload directory holding the triple
;
; Nothing here can reach the network, and nothing here is a
; profile-specific artifact: no provisioning installer, no runtime
; tree, no loose frontend file, ever.

#ifndef PWEB_PAYLOAD_DIR
  #error PWEB_PAYLOAD_DIR must be defined - include tools/setup/pwebappsetup.issi before this file, and build via a profile build script
#endif

[Files]
; the unchanged CAP-6 release triple - no loose frontend files, ever
Source: "{#PWEB_PAYLOAD_DIR}\releaseapp.exe"; DestDir: "{app}"; Flags: ignoreversion
Source: "{#PWEB_PAYLOAD_DIR}\app.pwb"; DestDir: "{app}"; Flags: ignoreversion
Source: "{#PWEB_PAYLOAD_DIR}\webview.dll"; DestDir: "{app}"; Flags: ignoreversion
